      "type": "explain",
      "title": "Vii° chord",
      "body": "The chord on the 7th degree is the **vii° chord**, a diminished triad. In C major it is B diminished, B D F.\n\n**Why it matters:** It shares two notes with V and pulls hard to I, so it can stand in for V. You will meet it again inside the dominant 7th chord in Unit 6.",
